        "original_id": "8d8587c1-ddc0-5e63-ad4f-330224fe68be",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giacomo Meyerbeer, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Works: L'esule di Granata, Serenade No. 6 for Orchestra in D major K. 239, Serenata notturna\n- Places: Salzburg\n- Topics: opera, Classical era\n\nFacts:\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was born on 27 January 1756 and was baptised as Johannes Chrysostomus Wolfgangus Theophilus Mozart.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was a prolific and influential composer of the Classical era.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart wrote the Serenade No. 6 for Orchestra in D major, K. 239, also called Serenata notturna, in Salzburg in 1776.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer was born as Jacob Liebmann Beer on 5 September 1791.\n- L'esule di Granata is a melodramma serio in two acts by Giacomo Meyerbeer.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer was a German opera composer of Jewish birth and has been described as perhaps the most successful stage composer of the nineteenth century.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart died on 5 December 1791.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer died on 2 May 1864.",
